@startuml
title Scenario Creation - Hypothetical Factory Method Design
caption OOAD design alternative - Not implemented in Deadlock Playground

left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam linetype ortho

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  FontColor #222222
}

package "Hypothetical Creator Hierarchy" {

  abstract class ScenarioCreator <<Creator>> {
    + createScenario(input): Scenario
    # makeScenario(input): Scenario
  }

  class FormScenarioCreator <<Concrete Creator>> {
    # makeScenario(input): Scenario
  }

  class ExampleScenarioCreator <<Concrete Creator>> {
    # makeScenario(input): Scenario
  }
}

package "Domain Product" {

  class Scenario <<Product>>

  class Process

  class Resource
}

class "Configuration Client" as Client <<Conceptual Client>>

ScenarioCreator <|-- FormScenarioCreator

ScenarioCreator <|-- ExampleScenarioCreator

Client --> ScenarioCreator : requests scenario creation

ScenarioCreator ..> Scenario : creates product

Scenario *-- Process : contains

Scenario *-- Resource : contains

note top of ScenarioCreator
  createScenario() defines
  the common creation workflow.

  makeScenario() is the
  Factory Method.

  Concrete creators override
  the factory method.
end note

note bottom of FormScenarioCreator
  Hypothetical implementation.

  Would construct a Scenario
  from validated form input.
end note

note bottom of ExampleScenarioCreator
  Hypothetical implementation.

  Illustrates an alternative
  creation mechanism.

  Example scenario loading is
  NOT implemented in the project.
end note

note bottom of Scenario
  The product remains the
  existing Scenario domain concept.

  Creation details are delegated
  to specialized creators.
end note

legend bottom
  HYPOTHETICAL OOAD DESIGN ONLY

  ScenarioCreator, FormScenarioCreator
  and ExampleScenarioCreator are proposed
  illustrative classes, not verified
  components of the current Java codebase.

  This diagram demonstrates the
  Factory Method design pattern.

  It does not document implemented features.
endlegend

@enduml
